WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
- All right, let's round out this hour

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.530
with just one more drop
of joy to add to your day.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.942
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:07.770
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:08.640
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.610
A New York woman has taken
her love of art, baking,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.210
and pop culture to new heights
by selling adorable cookies,

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.860
inspired by Rainn Wilson,
wishing you a happy birthday.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.670
Then there's this one
inspired by Leonardo DiCaprio

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:24.990
toasting the day.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:25.823
In fact,

00:00:25.823 --> 00:00:29.340
she serves up dozens of
culturally relevant designs.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.290
It's an intricate process
with a super clever

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.490
and delicious result, y'all.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.410
We have the owner of Funny Face Bakery

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.110
on the line right now
watching on NBC 4 New York.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.720
Everybody say hi to Sarah.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.840
(audience cheers)

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.451
What's up Sarah?
- Hey Kelly!

00:00:41.451 --> 00:00:42.284
Nice to meet you.

00:00:42.284 --> 00:00:43.920
- Nice to meet you as well.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.750
You are so talented. I love this idea.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.040
How'd you come up with it?

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:47.873
- Thank you.

00:00:47.873 --> 00:00:50.700
So I came up with it 2016.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.040
Originally, I wanted
to open New York City's

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.990
best cupcake bakery.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.580
About a week before,

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.530
I had an idea pop into my head

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.150
that a face belonged on a cookie.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.530
So I thought, okay,

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.600
I'll do this as like an opening day thing

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.670
and it was the primaries going on.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.190
So I did Hillary, Bernie, and Trump.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:11.520
Opening day comes and people
are going crazy over them.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.470
They instantly sell out.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.270
Everyone's Instagramming them.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.520
Next day, I set up all these cupcakes

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.160
and everyone's like
where are these cookies?

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.410
So I thought I had to shift my focus more

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:26.430
on like a trend pop culture cookie bakery.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.440
So if you walk into our store right now,

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.120
you'll see cookies that are keeping up

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.190
with the trends, memes.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.890
Right now we're seeing that
dark humor is really popular.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:38.580
So we have that cookie of like
the rainbow that says anxiety

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.580
and celebrities inspired by
like Taylor, Kim, and Harry.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.400
- Yeah, I love that.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.757
Harry's cookies could be
crazy, wild, and cool.

00:01:49.757 --> 00:01:50.970
(audience applauding)
I love his style.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:53.070
So a lot of work goes into each

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.600
and every cookie though, right?

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.433
- Oh yeah.

00:01:55.433 --> 00:01:56.880
A lot of love goes into them.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.520
So it starts out for like custom cookies.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.780
A customer will send a picture
of a face, an animal, a logo.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.130
Then we have a team of designers
that design the cookies.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:11.070
And after that's approved,
we make a cookie cutter,

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.120
we cut them out.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.320
Then we have a team of colorists
that matches up the colors.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.440
And once that's finished, we
do all the intricate details

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.300
like little tiny outlines,
draw like the eyes, the nose.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.133
- Wow.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:29.010
- So yeah, it's a minimum
of ordering 12 cookies.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.070
For even 12 cookies, it takes
like six to eight hours.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.320
So a lot of love goes into them.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.270
But I do wanna show you a cookie

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.400
that I'm really excited about.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.420
- All right.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.840
- It's a Kelly cookie!
- Yeah!

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.840
(audience cheering)

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.781
I want my cookie! That's amazing!

00:02:47.781 --> 00:02:50.640
It is crazy how talented
people are and stuff like that.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.850
I can't draw for anything
like, if to save my life.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.470
That is incredible.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.720
Like the rainbow with
anxiety is hilarious.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.980
It's my favorite one that you've showed,

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.960
other than my face. (laughs)

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:01.793
I love them!

00:03:01.793 --> 00:03:04.291
And thank you so much, Sarah,
for doing this for everyone.

00:03:04.291 --> 00:03:05.124
(audience applauding)

00:03:05.124 --> 00:03:05.970
It's such a cool business.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.520
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:10.439
All right.
(audience cheering)

00:03:10.439 --> 00:03:13.140
I have a little surprise
for someone in our audience,

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.790
courtesy of our season long partner Pilot,

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.050
pen makers of Frixion,

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.630
the go to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.010
There is a check.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.630
It's for a thousand dollars

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.220
and it's under someone's seat taped.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.540
So if you wanna look under your seat,

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.768
you might have that check.

00:03:25.768 --> 00:03:28.101
(drum roll)

00:03:29.159 --> 00:03:31.980
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.543
Who's got it? Who's got it?

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.153
Y'all are not looking!

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.143
It's taped. It's taped up under your seat.

00:03:44.768 --> 00:03:45.601
Yeah!

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:48.434
(audience cheers)

00:03:52.029 --> 00:03:54.030
Hi! You can stand up!

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:54.990
What's your name?

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.970
- Hi everyone. I'm Tiffany.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.940
- Tiffany, how are you
gonna use the money?

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.128
- Well, I graduated from
grad school recently. And-

00:04:03.128 --> 00:04:04.760
(audience cheering)

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.990
- Congratulations! That's awesome.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.010
- Thank you. I'm sorry.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.260
- Are you gonna use it for
more than paying off debt?

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.093
- I'm not sure.

00:04:11.093 --> 00:04:12.870
Yeah, maybe treat some people.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.869
I have a lot of friends.
- Treat yourself! Yes!

00:04:14.869 --> 00:04:16.680
(audience laughs)
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.630
Maybe come back and go to Universal

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.190
when I come back to your show.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:21.023
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:21.023 --> 00:04:23.229
Universal's so fun. You should do that.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.540
(audience laughs)
- Thank you so much.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.696
Sorry, I'm in shock. (laughs)

00:04:25.696 --> 00:04:27.330
(audience cheering)

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:28.979
- Alright, thank you to
all our guests this hour.

00:04:28.979 --> 00:04:32.940
Derek Hough, Jay Hernandez,
Shawn, Cristina, Alex, Daniel,

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.977
Nancy Alvarez, Stuart Moore,

00:04:34.977 --> 00:04:36.479
and a special thank you to all our friends

00:04:36.479 --> 00:04:37.830
at WESH 2 in Orlando.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:42.413
Y'all have a great day, and
if it's not, change anything.

